  '#', 
  '{"author":"Tone Pettit","source_publication":"The Accidental Intactivist", "date":"2026-10-09","abstract":"Yesterday in Portland, the State tried to legally downgrade bodily autonomy to a ''female privilege.'' They failed. We are going to trial on December 7th. Comparing my notes with Dr. Perry''s account reveals three shocking tactics the State used to defend the systemic denial of bodily autonomy for boys and intersex children:\n\n1. The Desperate Unnamed Expert Ploy: The State attempted to introduce an unnamed expert to invent a biological difference between male and female prepuce, which the judge struck from the record.\n2. Intersex Erasure: The State argued FGM laws only apply to females, erasing intersex children and relying on arbitrary birth assignment rather than inherent human rights.\n3. The ''Female Privilege'' Checkmate: The State argued that protection from non-consensual genital cutting is not a fundamental human right, but a ''female privilege'' granted by the government. \n\nWhile we wait for Judge Oden-Orr''s ruling, our mission remains unchanged: continue building the mountain of evidence they cannot ignore."}'
